<ModMetaData>
  <packageId>mandrake.rut.doctrine</packageId>
  <name>Jawa Doctrine Patches</name>
  <author>Mandrake</author>
  <supportedVersions><li>1.6</li></supportedVersions>
  <description>Campaign-doctrine patches: small, surgical changes that enforce the
Jawa design rules rather than rebalancing numbers.

Currently: removes the Droid Factory from the build menu. Droid parts, repair
and upgrading are deliberately untouched. The Jawa restore droids; they do not
manufacture them.

Assemblies/JawaDoctrineCore.dll (DROIDWORKS_ISFLESH_RELATIONS_CRASH_1, 2026-08-30):
one Harmony postfix on PawnComponentsUtility.CreateInitialComponents, allocating
pawn.relations for Humanlike + non-flesh pawns (vanilla only allocates it for
IsFlesh pawns) — the gap DroidsAreMachines.xml's own isOrganic:false opens for
every droid race project-wide.

Rationale lives in worldbuilding/balance_paradigm.md (Axis 18a/18b).
Load last.</description>

  <!-- LOAD ORDER, 2026-08-13. There was none declared here at all, and the
       RimSort user rule named ONE mod (Outer Rim - Droid Depot). That was short
       by a factor of forty: MegafaunaYield.xml alone carries 630 defNames
       grouped into 42 PatchOperationFindMod blocks, and DroidsAreMachines.xml
       rewrites flesh types belonging to Asimov and ABF: Synstructs Core.

       A PatchOperationFindMod checks that a mod is PRESENT. It does not order
       anything. Loaded before its target, every operation in the group matches
       nothing and is skipped with one log line among thousands - the patch is
       inert and looks fine. That is why this list is long rather than tidy.

       Every packageId below was resolved from the donor's own About.xml with
       src/RimMandrake/Utils/build_packageid_index.py, which strips
       <modDependencies> before matching - reading the first <packageId> in the
       file returns a DEPENDENCY's id and has produced wrong answers here before.

       Deliberately absent:
        * Core, Biotech, Anomaly and Odyssey - base game and DLC always load
          first, so a loadAfter naming them buys nothing.
        * "Mythological Creatures!" - MegafaunaYield has a group for it, but no
          such mod is installed today. A loadAfter naming a packageId that does
          not exist fails SILENTLY and constrains nothing, which is exactly how
          mandrake.rsw.armoury's rule sat inert. Its patch group is a harmless
          no-op; if the mod is ever reinstalled, add it here.
        * Megafauna (Spino.Megafauna), Beasts of the Rim (Mlie.BeastsoftheRim),
          Mythic Ages: Megafauna Bestiary
          (veterano.mythicages.megafaunabestiary) and Jurassic Rimworld -
          Dinosaurs Only (Mlie.JurassicRimworldDinosaursOnly) - RETIRED
          2026-09-05 on the owner's ruling; see
          design/Jawa/worldbuilding/mod_retirement_audit.md and
          design/Jawa/worldbuilding/RETIREMENT_CHECKLIST.md. Their
          MegafaunaYield groups were deleted with them.
        * Grimstone : Beasts (Abrolo.Grimstone.Beasts), ReGrowth: Boiling
          (ReGrowth.BOTR.BoilingForest), Titans (titans.fl), Vanilla Animals
          Expanded (VanillaExpanded.VanillaAnimalsExpanded) and Giant Snake
          (Continued) (zal.giantsnake) - REMOVED 2026-09-06 (dirty-review
          pass, WEAPONTAGS_RENORMALISE_STALE_DEFS_1's sibling finding): none
          of the five is in the live ModsConfig.xml, and MegafaunaYield.xml
          has no group for any of them either - the megafauna groups these
          five belonged to were already deleted, this loadAfter list just
          wasn't trimmed to match. A loadAfter naming an absent packageId is
          a silent no-op (see the PatchOperationFindMod note above), so this
          was never a live bug, only stale bookkeeping. -->
